$\\pi^+$ transverse momentum, and Bj\\\"{o}rken $x$. Also shown are the published result from the 6 GeV experiment~\\cite{xqian}. Bottom panel: the projected measurement for the Sivers asymmetry for $\\pi^-$ together with the published results from ~\\cite{xqian}.","filename":"SoLID_pim_sivers_NoTheo.png"},{"key":"11a64d56ae967332039f55c43c08d20b","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/11a64d56ae967332039f55c43c08d20b","source":"arxiv","caption":"Top panel: The projected Jefferson Lab 12-GeV SoLID determination of the tensor charge of u and d quark (black points) together with model dependent extractions of these quantities based on the existing data. Also shown are predictions from lattice QCD, Dyson-Schwinger Equations, and various models. Bottom panel: The projected pretzelocity asymmetry measurement from a transversely polarized $^3$He target (``neutron'') together with predictions from Boffi and Pasquini {\\it et al.}~\\cite{pasquini2009} at a $Q^2$ value of 2.5 GeV$^2$.","filename":"FigTensorHG_WP.png"},{"key":"dcaffb9286af16d7a0e2ca1ce46ac27b","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/dcaffb9286af16d7a0e2ca1ce46ac27b","source":"arxiv","caption":"Top panel: The projected Jefferson Lab 12-GeV SoLID determination of the tensor charge of u and d quark (black points) together with model dependent extractions of these quantities based on the existing data. Also shown are predictions from lattice QCD, Dyson-Schwinger Equations, and various models. Bottom panel: The projected pretzelocity asymmetry measurement from a transversely polarized $^3$He target (``neutron'') together with predictions from Boffi and Pasquini {\\it et al.}~\\cite{pasquini2009} at a $Q^2$ value of 2.5 GeV$^2$.","filename":"SoLID_neutron_both_pretz_AllQ2_big.png"},{"key":"6a471769e07c6221b96acc54984926ca","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/6a471769e07c6221b96acc54984926ca","source":"arxiv","caption":"Left panel: Projected uncertainties for $A_{PV}$ in percent as a function of kinematics. The green points are from 11 GeV beam and the yellow points are from 6.6 GeV beam. Right panel: Projected mass limits for composite models. The purple ellipse shows the mass limits from the 6 GeV PVDIS results in combination with the published $C_{1q}$ results from PVES (including QWeak) and atomic parity violation experiments. The orange ellipse shows the mass limits from the SoLID-PVDIS projection in combination with the same projected $C_{1q}$ results including the estimated sensitivity from the full Qweak data sample.","filename":"deu_BinErrors_crop.png"},{"key":"c245575cc336a139969b4d8f2cc11095","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/c245575cc336a139969b4d8f2cc11095","source":"arxiv","caption":"Left panel: Projected uncertainties for $A_{PV}$ in percent as a function of kinematics. The green points are from 11 GeV beam and the yellow points are from 6.6 GeV beam. Right panel: Projected mass limits for composite models. The purple ellipse shows the mass limits from the 6 GeV PVDIS results in combination with the published $C_{1q}$ results from PVES (including QWeak) and atomic parity violation experiments. The orange ellipse shows the mass limits from the SoLID-PVDIS projection in combination with the same projected $C_{1q}$ results including the estimated sensitivity from the full Qweak data sample.","filename":"mass_limits_C_crop.png"},{"key":"0bc43ad3e6b16ce9cbba85f1f515d8da","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/0bc43ad3e6b16ce9cbba85f1f515d8da","source":"arxiv","caption":"Total  $J/\\psi$  photoproduction cross section versus photon energy in the threshold region, except for the proposed electroproduction measurement (filled red circles) where the data are plotted as a function of the equivalent photon energy.","filename":"figure_2_wp_jpsi.png"}],"license":[{"url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","imposing":"arXiv"}],"texkeys":["Chen:2014psa"],"citeable":true,"keywords":[{"value":"electron nucleus: deep inelastic scattering","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"deep inelastic scattering: semi-inclusive reaction","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"effect: higher-twist","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"parity: violation","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"charge: symmetry","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"energy: upgrade","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"parton: distribution function","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"Newport News CEBAF Linac","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"helium: nuclide","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"deuteron","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"polarized target: transverse","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"transverse momentum dependence","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"pi: electroproduction","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"spectrometer: proposed","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"J/psi(3100): electroproduction","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"threshold","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"proposed experiment","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"12 GeV","schema":"INSPIRE"}],"abstracts":[{"value":"In order to fully exploit the physics potential of Jefferson Lab after 12 GeV energy upgrade, a new Solenoidal Large Acceptance Device (SoLID) is proposed. The SoLID spectrometer, with its unique capability of large acceptance and high luminosity, is ideal for precision measurements in semi-inclusive DIS to study transverse spin and transverse-momentum-dependent parton distributions of the nucleon, and for parity-violating Deep Inelastic Scattering (DIS) to perform precision tests of the Standard Model at low energy as well as addressing specific issues in nucleon structure including charge symmetry violation, d/u ratio and higher-twist effects due to di-quark. SoLID is also essential for precision measurements of J/\\psi electroproduction in the threshold region to study non-perturbative gluon dynamics and interaction. Five highly rated SoLID experiments and two \"run group\" experiments have been approved by the JLab Physics Advisory Committee. The physics program is presented along with an overview of the SoLID instrumentation and its current status.","source":"arXiv"}],"references":[{"reference":{"misc":["The SoLID Collaboration, SoLID (Solenoidal Large Intensity Device) Preliminary Conceptual Design Report, May"],"urls":[{"value":"http://hallaweb.jlab.org/12GeV/SoLID/dowload/doc/solid_precdr.pdf"}],"label":"1","publication_info":{"year":2014}}},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/902486"},"reference":{"label":"2","authors":[{"full_name":"Qian, X."}],"publication_info":{"year":2011,"artid":"072003","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.Lett.","journal_volume":"107"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1223997"},"reference":{"label":"3","authors":[{"full_name":"Anselmino, M."},{"full_name":"Boglione, M."},{"full_name":"D'Alesio, U."},{"full_name":"Melis, S."},{"full_name":"Murgia, F."},{"full_name":"Prokudin, A."}],"publication_info":{"year":2013,"artid":"094019","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.D","journal_volume":"87"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/806038"},"reference":{"label":"4","authors":[{"full_name":"Anselmino, M."},{"full_name":"Boglione, M."},{"full_name":"D'Alesio, U."},{"full_name":"Kotzinian, A."},{"full_name":"Melis, S."},{"full_name":"Murgia, F."},{"full_name":"Prokudin, A."}],"publication_info":{"year":2009,"artid":"98","page_start":"98","journal_title":"Nucl.Phys.B Proc.Suppl.","journal_volume":"191"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1207450"},"reference":{"label":"5","authors":[{"full_name":"Bacchetta, A."},{"full_name":"Courtoy, A."},{"full_name":"Radici, M."}],"publication_info":{"year":2013,"artid":"119","page_start":"119","journal_title":"JHEP","journal_volume":"03"}},"curated_relation":false},{"reference":{"misc":["private communications"],"label":"6","authors":[{"full_name":"Prokudin, A."}]}},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1327738"},"reference":{"misc":["Ch. Kallidonis, G Koutsou (ETM Collaboration), to appear in"],"label":"